# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Build output (note: build/ itself is source, only its output is ignored)
/dist/
# PyInstaller's scratch area, which `build/build.py` points at with --workpath so
# that nothing it writes lands beside the spec file it is building from.
/build/pyinstaller/

# Bundled binaries. Not tracked: pinned in build/ffmpeg.lock.json and fetched with
# `python build/fetch_ffmpeg.py`. See proingest/resources/ffmpeg/PROVENANCE.md.
# Ignore the whole folder and re-admit the two files that are source, because the macOS
# binaries are named `ffmpeg` and `ffprobe` with no extension: an `*.exe` rule stopped
# covering them the moment the target changed, and they are 132 MB.
proingest/resources/ffmpeg/*
!proingest/resources/ffmpeg/PROVENANCE.md
!proingest/resources/ffmpeg/LICENSE.ffmpeg.txt

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# User data
*.pibatch
*.pibatch.bak

# Manager-facing plan the user keeps outside git. Was untracked by convention alone until
# a `git add docs/` swept it in; convention is not enforcement.
/docs/ROADMAP.md
/docs/ROADMAP.docx

# Front-end mock of the UI, for showing producers. Deliberately untracked at the user's
# request: it is a picture of docs/UI_SPEC.md, never a second implementation, and the spec
# is what the repo carries. Still on disk, still published as an artifact; see PROGRESS
# section 8.
/preview/

# WSL NTFS alternate data stream artifacts
*:Zone.Identifier

# A real sample turnover the user dropped into the working tree on 2026-09-19: five
# Resolve-trimmed camera files, 775 MB, plus a .drt and a metadata CSV. It is evidence for
# the respec, not source, and one `git add .` would put the media in history for good.
# Re-exported 2026-09-22 with the metadata filled in. It briefly carried the name
# Turnover199_ForBEN/ and was renamed back; that pattern stays as a guard, so a clone that
# still has the old name cannot un-ignore 775 MB of media into a `git add .`.
/Turnover199/
/Turnover199_ForBEN/
